# Books to Scrape — Parsel Web Scraper

This project scrapes 120 books from books.toscrape.com using Python, requests,
and Parsel. 

## Fields collected

- Book title
- Price
- Availability
- Rating
- Category
- Product-page URL

## Tools used

- Google Colab
- Python
- requests
- Parsel
- CSV

## How to run

1. Open the notebook in Google Colab.
2. Run:

```python
!pip install requests parsel
```

3. Run the scraper cell.
4. The script creates and downloads `books.csv`.

## Approach

The scraper starts from the first catalogue page, extracts book data from each
`article.product_pod` element, and follows the “Next” pagination link until it
collects 120 unique books.

Since category is not available on the catalogue page, the scraper visits each
product page and extracts the category from the breadcrumb navigation.

## Error handling

- HTTP request retries
- Request timeout
- Duplicate URL removal
- Missing-field handling
- One-second delay between requests
- Progress logging

## Challenge

The category is only available on individual product pages, so each product URL
had to be visited separately. Relative links were converted to absolute URLs
using `urljoin`.
